# Security rules for murmur

Version: 2026-11-06

murmur is a static website and an Electron and iPhone app, with no server, no database, and no accounts. The rules for those do not apply here; these do.

## Before any site deploy

Run the outside check. 0 FAIL is the bar, and every WARN gets a fix or a written reason.

```bash
node scripts/posture-check.mjs https://murmurapp.app --repo .
```

- All 6 graded headers and COOP come from `site/headers.js`, and `Access-Control-Expose-Headers` lists them.
- No `unsafe-inline` or `unsafe-eval`: the site has no inline script or style attribute.
- `/.well-known/security.txt` has a Contact and an Expires within a year.
- Fingerprinted files are cached a year and always linked with `?v=`. HTML revalidates.
- No third-party script, tracker, or cookie, so there is no consent banner to need.
- SPF and DMARC stay on the domain.
- Scan `https://`, never `http://`.

## In the app

- Renderers stay sandboxed: contextIsolation on, no nodeIntegration, every IPC channel on a preload allowlist.
- Windows load only bundled pages; navigation and permission requests stay locked.
- Main-process requests go through `appFetch`.
- The API key stays encrypted at rest with safeStorage, and is never logged.
- Logs hold no dictated words.
- No native modules that need compiling.
- The formatter fails open. Dictated text is content, never instructions.
- Nothing new leaves the device without changing `/privacy/` first.

## Keys and secrets

- Never commit, log, or paste a secret. LaBroi types secret values himself.
- Signing keys, the notary key, and the license key stay outside the repo.
- Rotate a key on any suspicion. `INCIDENT_RESPONSE.md` has the runbooks.

## Automation

- Every GitHub Action is pinned to a commit, with the least permission it needs.
- Updates from Dependabot get read, not merged blindly.
- Commit the lockfile. Never `npm audit fix`; bump the 1 package.

## Privacy

- `/privacy/` states a period or a test for every kind of record. Changing a period means changing the page, and LaBroi signs off.
- A new thing leaving the device changes the privacy page and the App Store label first.
- Never commit a real dictation, a scan report, or a vendor's review. `security-audits/` stays local.
- A take someone reports becomes a test case only with their yes, rewritten without names or details.

## Recurring

| When | What |
|---|---|
| Every push and PR | CI, CodeQL |
| Weekly | Outside check, an issue on failure; Dependabot |
| Every year | Review `INCIDENT_RESPONSE.md`, confirm who can publish a release |
| After an incident | A written review, and a lesson in the security-hardening skill |

## Ask LaBroi first

Policy wording and retention periods, repo and account settings, deleting keys or data, rewriting git history, and anything that changes what leaves a device.
